{
  "families": [
    {
      "family": "pipelined",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 11, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 8, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.2,
      "why": "Baseline pipelined family: one register per micro-rotation. Provides a reference for area and accuracy. Likely dominated by pipelined_m in area, but useful to confirm and to map the front if pipelined_m has unexpected LUT overhead."
    },
    {
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 11, "high": 18, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 8, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "m", "low": 2, "high": 8, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.8,
      "why": "Most promising for the min area objective. By registering every m stages, it reduces FF count while keeping the same datapath LUTs. The m parameter trades Fmax (not a constraint beyond 1 MSPS) for area. Allocating the majority of the budget here to thoroughly explore the accuracy-area trade-off."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec requires throughput >= 1 MSPS, which both pipelined families easily meet (1 result/cycle). The critical constraint is max_abs_err <= 2^-10, which requires data_width >= 11 because the output LSB is 2^-(W-2). To minimize area (LUTs+FFs), we focus on pipelined_m, which can reduce FF count by a factor of m without increasing LUTs. We allocate 80% of the budget to pipelined_m to explore the m parameter and the accuracy-area trade-off, and 20% to pipelined as a baseline. The parameter ranges cover the feasible region: data_width 11..18 (11 is the minimum for accuracy, 18 allows higher accuracy), n_iter 8..20 (8 to test low iteration with high guards, 20 for high accuracy), angle_guard -2..4 and frac_guard 0..4 (full registry ranges to allow trade-offs), rounding both. For pipelined_m, m from 2..8 explores the FF reduction vs. combinational delay trade-off."
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "next_plan": null,
  "rationale": "Final round, budget/round cap reached, so this is a stop. The feasible front already brackets the selection objective well: its cheapest point pipelined_m [W=18 N=12 angle_guard=-1 frac_guard=0 trunc m=7] has luts_plus_ffs=847, meets throughput (59.6 MSPS >= 1) and error (2^-10.71 <= 2^-10), and is the min-luts_plus_ffs pick the spec's selection rule would choose. Both constraints are comfortably satisfiable (0% throughput violations, max_abs_err 2^-10.71 at the selection corner vs the 2^-10 limit), so infeasible is not warranted. The front spans luts_plus_ffs 847..1367 and accuracy_bits 10.7..13.6 (HV 1541 vs ref 1500), with the low-area corner far from any constraint boundary — refining further would not change the selected design, and no unexplored families remain."
}
